    "product": {
      "id": 1161320,
      "name": "Green Italian Frying Pepper",
      "description": "The Italian \"friggi friggi\" pepper is more commonly known as friggitelli , or Italian frying peppers. They are mild, small, and slender peppers native to southern Italy, prized for their sweet flavor and thin skin that makes them ideal for frying. The name comes from the Italian verb friggere , meaning \"to fry\". Friggitelli have a slightly sweet, fruity, and mild flavor, with a low heat level of 100–500 on the Scoville scale. Some varieties are entirely heatless. The taste can have a pleasant, slightly bitter edge.",
